{"agent":"lane-rec-surface","data":{"by":"lane-rec-surface","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"Adding `\"correct\"` to the help-topic list introduces a new topic that has no corresponding help template in the change: the manifest contains only a modified `ddflow/templates/prompts/help/update.md`, not a new `ddflow/templates/prompts/help/correct.md`. With the existing topic/template convention, `ddflow help correct` will look for the missing `correct.md` template and fail (or return no help), while `ddflow help update` is the only place the new correction guidance actually exists.","digest":"6a12f066da6c809f","location":"ddflow/services/help.py:91","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/help.py:91"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new common-field loop in `_h_updated` assigns `author_model` whenever the key is present, including when its value is falsey (`None` or `\"\"`). The completion branch immediately below then tries to ignore falsey author values with `ev.data.get(\"author_model\") or ev.data.get(\"author_family\") or it.author_model`, but that fallback can no longer recover the previous author because the common loop has already overwritten `it.author_model` with the falsey value. Given an update/completion event whose data contains `{\"author_model\": \"\"}` or `{\"author_model\": null}` (for example, an unknown/omitted author serialized as empty), the item’s recorded author_model is cleared instead of preserved, contrary to the `or` fallback’s intent.","digest":"027523b3e4f49acd","location":"ddflow/core/handlers/items.py:_h_updated","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/handlers/items.py:_h_updated"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`_text_of` only catches `OSError` when reading `--from-file`. If the file exists and is readable but its bytes are not valid in the default encoding, `Path(path).read_text()` raises `UnicodeDecodeError` (a `ValueError`, not an `OSError`). For example, `ddflow correct BUG-1 --field body --from-file /tmp/binary.bin --reason 